- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y=-8 \\\\ x-3y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320836/field-1" "q-320836/field-2" "q-320836/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
